    {
      "id": "E-h",
      "verdict": "INCONCLUSIVE",
      "binds": [
        "cloud"
      ],
      "measured": {
        "blocked": "ATTEMPTED",
        "reason": "harness defect: one user access token was exported for a probe that runs about two hours; it expired during point 3's create (HTTP 401) and the writer exited before its kill point. Points 1 and 2 matched the premise (plan proposes the create, retry failed ALREADY_EXISTS, one cluster), but their import into a copy of the state never ran (tofu import argument order). Both defects are fixed; a rerun needs its own approval."
      },
      "tofu_version": "1.10.10",
      "provider_version": "8.4.0",
      "date": "2026-11-23",
      "transcript_sha256": "c0b9ac0138605ccdca028d0911c1a0d561ec14b435a2e99a163e3b1a412b3ff5"
    },
    {
      "id": "E-i",
      "verdict": "INCONCLUSIVE",
      "binds": [
        "cloud"
      ],
      "measured": {
        "blocked": "ATTEMPTED",
        "reason": "calibration: GKE refused actAs of the foreign identity with HTTP 400 'The user does not have access to service account', a wording the refusal classifier did not recognise, so no verdict. Every other refuse path was refused with the operator control succeeding, the must_succeed calibration (actAs the designated node identity) passed, and legacy ABAC and disabling workload identity were open as designed. The candidate role file named five container.nodePools.* permissions IAM does not have; the run used the nine valid ones. A rerun needs its own approval."
      },
      "tofu_version": "1.10.10",
